• ## Executive verdict

  Unumae’s philosophy is unusually well protected at the architecture level: equal selection, one Human per cycle, guest access, no followers, no popularity ranking, no infinite feed,
  private Remember counts, and permanent chronological archiving are all taken seriously.

  However, the product is not yet end-to-end complete enough for public beta. Several features described as “implemented” are database foundations or isolated screens that a real user
  cannot successfully reach or finish.

  Most importantly:

  > The audience half of Unumae largely exists. The selected Human’s half of the core loop does not.

  I would not launch a public beta until the selected-person journey, answering flow, moderation actions, notifications, and privacy defects below are fixed.

  No source files were changed during this audit.

